            <ArticleTitle>Rhodium-catalyzed benzoisothiazole synthesis by tandem annulation reactions of sulfoximines and activated olefins.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9983-9986</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02586f</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rhodium(iii)-catalyzed N-directed ortho C-H activation reactions have been developed for the synthesis of unique heterocyclic benzoisothiazoles. Herein, this novel tandem annulation approach can efficiently construct benzoisothiazole compounds from free NH-sulfoximines and alkenes via C-H activation, olefination and subsequent intramolecular aza-Michael cyclization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
